  "aiGuidance": {
    "purpose": "Create a bounded argument decision. Keep navigation separate: contains is never causal decomposition; requires-argument is used only where a selected option requires a narrower argument.\n\n## Name the primary audience\nEvery argument must name the one primary person who needs to understand, use, challenge or carry this decision. Use a concrete role and context. Do not confuse this with the owner, formal authority, affected people or a marketing segment.\n\n## Give each record a title\nEvery option-consideration, argument-test and argument-review record, and every causal record (observation, diagnosis, premise, hypothesis, mechanism, condition, activity, project, outcome, impact) the argument produces, carries a `title`: a short noun phrase naming it, distinct from its siblings, keeping any hedge the record carries. Options, arguments and indicators already label by their own title; their code stays the stable id. See each type's aiGuidance."
  },
